| 2026-05-04 | 1B | CRITICAL | Android-Avalonia connection broken: PairingClient.cs used old simple HMAC while PairingService.cs was upgraded to ECDH X25519 | Upgraded PairingClient.cs to ECDH X25519 via NSec with HKDF-SHA256; updated AndroidNativeExports.cs method signature; verified infrastructure (PinnedHostStore, navigation flow) already complete |
| 2026-05-04 | 1B | HIGH | Access key system incomplete removal causing config mismatch | Removed RequireAccessKey and AccessKey from RemexHostSettings, cleaned appsettings.json, updated SECURITY.md documentation, added AllowFirstTimePairing property |
| 2026-05-04 | 1A+1C | COMPLETE | Track 1 finalization: TCP SslStream + .NET desktop pairing | Wrapped RemexNetworkListener TCP socket in SslStream with TLS 1.3; implemented .NET desktop ConnectionViewModel pairing flow with PairingDialog UI; added localization strings Status_Pairing and Pairing_InvalidPin; removed access key from BuildWebSocketUri |
| 2026-05-03 | 2C | LOW | MaterialShapes.* not available in Material3 1.4.0 stable | Replaced with RoundedPolygon shapes from androidx.graphics.shapes 1.1.0 |
| 2026-05-03 | 2F | HIGH | google-services.json missing from repo | Crashlytics deferred; noted as blocked |
| 2026-05-03 | 2A | LOW | Android download destination not implemented (SAF) | File download POSTs to host; receiving chunks requires Android SAF integration in future sprint |
| 2026-05-06 | 2A | HIGH | Shared-root design requires host-side path boundary changes; current implementation still exposes raw remote paths | Reworking Track 2A to root-relative browse/transfer and improved desktop/Android product flow |
| 2026-05-06 | 2A | MEDIUM | True pair-level host permissions are blocked by the current security backbone lacking a durable client identity on the host | Current slice uses host-level shared roots; per-pair permissions need a follow-up identity contract and host settings UI |
| 2026-05-06 | 2A | LOW | Reverse mobile-folder browsing from desktop would require new host-mediated cross-client routing and Android shared-root exposure | Deferred beyond 2.0; current release focus is polishing host-side shared-folder transfer UX |
